[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 22. Let's try to determine the inner product <x, x'> for x ≠ x'. From ||x - x'||² = d², we have <x, x'> = (||x||² + ||x'||² - d²)/2.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 23. Now, we want to find y such that for all x in S, ||x - y||² = d²/2.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122]     Expand: ||x||² - 2<x, y> + ||y||² = d²/2   => <x, y> = (||x||² + ||y||² - d²/2)/2   ...(9)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 24. Also, for orthogonality, for x ≠ x', <x-y, x'-y> = 0 => <x, x'> - <x,y> - <x',y> + ||y||² = 0.
