[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 34. Another idea: Use the fact that in a Hilbert space, the closed convex hull of S is well-defined. Let C be the closed convex hull of S. I claim that the point y we are looking for is the unique point in C that is equidistant from all points in S. In fact, for a simplex, the center of the circumsphere is such a point. For an infinite set, we can define y as the limit of centers for finite subsets.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
