[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 37. Insight from finite dimension: For a regular simplex in R^n with side length d, the circumradius is R = d * sqrt(n/(2(n+1)) ). As n->infty, R-> d/√2. So in the infinite-dimensional case, the circumsphere has radius d/√2.
