[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 2. The length of the midsegment (joining midpoints of legs) is the average of the bases: m = (b1 + b2)/2
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 3. For a segment parallel to the bases that divides the area in a given ratio, we use similar trapezoids and area formulas
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 4. The ratio of areas of similar figures is the square of the ratio of corresponding lengths
