[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Similarly, new non-promoted group: size = Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Their total new score = (total old score of Y) + 5Y = \( S_Y + 5Y \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] And this equals \( 59Y \)  => (5)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] But note: \( S_R = S_X + S_Y = 56(X+Y) \)  => (3)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Also, the X students have scores between 60 and 64 inclusive. So \( S_X \) is between 60X and 64X.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Similarly, Y students have scores <60, so at most 59. So \( S_Y <= 59Y \).
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] From (5): \( S_Y + 5Y = 59Y \)  => \( S_Y = 54Y \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] So the average of the Y students originally was 54.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] From (3): \( S_X = 56(X+Y) - S_Y = 56X + 56Y - 54Y = 56X + 2Y \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] But also, since X students have scores between 60 and 64, \( 60X <= S_X <= 64X \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] So \( 60X <= 56X + 2Y <= 64X \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => \( 4X <= 2Y <= 8X \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => \( 2X <= Y <= 4X \)   (A)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Now from (4):
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] \( S_P + S_X + 5(P_1+X) = 75(P_1+X) \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => \( S_P + S_X = 70(P_1+X) \)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] But \( S_P = 71P_1 \), so:
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 71P_1 + S_X = 70P_1 + 70X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => S_X = 70X - P_1   (6)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] But we also have S_X = 56X + 2Y from above.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] So: 56X + 2Y = 70X - P_1
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => 2Y = 14X - P_1
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => P_1 = 14X - 2Y   (7)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Now from (1):
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] S_P + S_R = 66N
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 71P_1 + 56(X+Y) = 66(P_1 + X + Y)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 71P_1 + 56X + 56Y = 66P_1 + 66X + 66Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 5P_1 = 10X + 10Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] P_1 = 2X + 2Y   (8)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Now equate (7) and (8):
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 14X - 2Y = 2X + 2Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 12X = 4Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 3X = Y   (9)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] So Y = 3X.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Then from (8): P_1 = 2X + 2*(3X) = 8X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] And from (A): Y should be between 2X and 4X. 3X is within [2X,4X], so valid.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Now N = P_1 + X + Y = 8X + X + 3X = 12X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] And N < 40, so 12X < 40 => X < 40/12 ~ 3.33, so X=1,2,3.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Thus N = 12, 24, 36.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Now for part (b): after increase, promoted average becomes 79 and non-promoted becomes 47.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] So similarly:
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] New promoted avg = 79, size = P_1 + X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] New non-promoted avg = 47, size = Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Then from (5) equivalent: S_Y + 5Y = 47Y  => S_Y = 42Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] Then S_X = 56(X+Y) - S_Y = 56X + 56Y - 42Y = 56X + 14Y
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] And constraint: 60X <= S_X <= 64X  => 60X <= 56X + 14Y <= 64X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => 4X <= 14Y <= 8X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => (2/7)X <= Y <= (4/7)X   (B)  [since 14Y>=4X => Y>= (4/14)X = (2/7)X, and 14Y<=8X => Y<= (8/14)X=(4/7)X]
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] From (4) equivalent: S_P + S_X + 5(P_1+X) = 79(P_1+X)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] => S_P + S_X = 74(P_1+X)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 71P_1 + S_X = 74P_1 + 74X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] S_X = 74X + 3P_1   (6b)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] But S_X = 56X + 14Y, so:
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 56X + 14Y = 74X + 3P_1
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 14Y = 18X + 3P_1
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 3P_1 = 14Y - 18X
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] P_1 = (14Y - 18X)/3   (7b)
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 
