[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] For part (a):
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 1. Define variables: Let X = number of originally repeaters who have scores between 60 and 64 (so become promoted after +5), Y = number of originally repeaters with scores <60 (remain non-promoted after +5), P1 = number originally promoted.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 2. Write equations from original averages: overall, promoted, repeaters.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 3. Write equations from new averages after +5 for the new promoted and new non-promoted groups.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 4. Express S_X and S_Y in terms of X and Y.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 5. Use the constraints on S_X (60X to 64X) and S_Y (<=59Y) to derive inequalities.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 6. Solve the system to get relations P1=8X, Y=3X, N=12X.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:36 run_experiments.py:122] 7. Since N<40, X=1,2,3 so N=12,24,36.
