[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] $\mu_{p}=1.41 \times 10^{-26} \mathrm{~J} / \mathrm{T}$. Let the hydrogen atom be in the ground state, meaning $\Psi(\mathbf{r})=\frac{e^{-r / a_{0}}}{\sqrt{\pi a_{0}^{3}}}$, where $a_{0}=5.29 \times 10^{-11} \mathrm{~m}$ is the Bohr radius. Evaluate the magnitude of the integral $|\mathbf{I}|$ (in SI units).
