[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] 14. Then v_rms = sqrt(3kT/m) = sqrt(3 * k * (sqrt(2) ΔE_rms / k) / m) = sqrt( (3 sqrt(2) ΔE_rms) / m ). This is a direct formula.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] 15. We will calculate v_rms using this formula, and T is already found.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] So the high-level strategy is:
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] a) Use the derived relationship ΔE_rms = kT / sqrt(2) to calculate T.
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] b) Use the formula v_rms = sqrt(3kT/m) to calculate the rms speed of Be nuclei. The mass m is for Be-9 (9 atomic mass units).
[INFO] 09-21 22:29:37 run_experiments.py:122] c) The temperature T calculated in step (a) is the estimate for Tc.
