[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 1. Splitting the integral of f into two parts: from 0 to a and from a to ∞.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 2. Applying the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality to bound ∫₀ᵃ f(x) dx ≤ √(∫₀ᵃ f(x)² dx · ∫₀ᵃ 1 dx) ≤ √(B a), where B = ∫₀∞ f(x)² dx.
