[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 4. Combining these to get ∫₀∞ f(x) dx ≤ √(B a) + C/a for any a > 0.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 5. Minimizing the right-hand side over a > 0 using calculus (or AM-GM) to find the optimal a and the resulting bound.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 6. Cubing the bound and comparing constants (27/4 < 8) to establish the desired inequality.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] **Pitfall Prediction**:
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] - *Conceptual Trap*: Misapplying Cauchy-Schwarz (e.g., using an incorrect weight function or missing the nonnegativity of f).
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] - *Calculation Trap*: Incorrectly solving for the minimizing a (e.g., mishandling exponents in a = (2C/√B)^(2/3)).
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] - *Completeness Trap*: Forgetting to cube the final bound or failing to justify why 27/4 ≤ 8 suffices.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] **Strategy Formulation**:
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 1. Split ∫₀∞ f(x) dx into ∫₀ᵃ f(x) dx + ∫ₐ∞ f(x) dx.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 2. Use Cauchy-Schwarz on ∫₀ᵃ f(x) dx to bound it by √(B a).
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 3. Use the inequality 1 ≤ x/a for x ≥ a to bound ∫ₐ∞ f(x) dx by C/a.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 4. Combine to get ∫₀∞ f(x) dx ≤ √(B a) + C/a.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 5. Minimize g(a) = √(B a) + C/a by setting derivative dg/da = (√B)/(2√a) - C/a² = 0, yielding a = (2C/√B)^(2/3).
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 6. Substitute a into g(a) to get the optimal bound: 3·2^(-2/3)(BC)^(1/3).
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 7. Cube both sides: (∫ f dx)³ ≤ (27/4) B C.
[INFO] 09-22 03:31:23 run_experiments.py:122] 8. Since 27/4 < 8, the inequality (∫ f dx)³ ≤ 8 B C holds.
