[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 1. The midsegment of a trapezoid is parallel to the bases and has length equal to the average of the two bases.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 2. A segment parallel to the bases divides a trapezoid into two trapezoids with proportional heights.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 3. The area of a trapezoid is (1/2) × height × (sum of parallel sides).
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 4. The ratio of areas of similar geometric figures equals the square of the ratio of their corresponding linear dimensions.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 
