[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - *Conceptual Trap*: Confusing the midsegment (which joins midpoints of legs) with the segment that creates equal areas. These are different segments.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - *Calculation Trap*: Incorrectly setting up the area ratio equations. The areas of the two regions created by the midsegment are in ratio 2:3, but the segment x creates equal areas.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - *Completeness Trap*: Failing to convert from the ratio of areas to the position of segment x, or not calculating x²/100 correctly at the end.
