[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - Conceptual Trap: Misunderstanding what makes a set sparse - it's about the count of strings at each length, not the total size.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - Calculation Trap: When combining multiple sparse sets, we need to ensure the resulting set remains sparse (the polynomial bound still applies).
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - Completeness Trap: For part 2, failing to consider both directions of the equality (⊆ and ⊇) when comparing complexity classes.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] - Conceptual Trap: Confusing P_angel with NP. In NP, each input has its own witness, but in P_angel, all strings of the same length share the same angel string.
