[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 开始处理问题： Consider the following two person game. A number of pebbles are situated on the table. Two players make their moves alternately. A move consists of taking off the table  $x$  pebbles where  $x$  is the square of any positive integer. The player who is unable to make a move loses. Prove that there are infinitely many initial situations in which the second player can win no matter how his opponent plays.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 正在获取解决方案计划...
