[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 1. First, analyze what σ(a^n) looks like for different types of a (prime vs composite).
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 2. For a prime p, σ(p^n) = (p^(n+1) - 1)/(p - 1) = 1 + p + p^2 + ... + p^n.
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:53 run_experiments.py:122] 3. For σ(a^n) - 1 to be divisible by 2021, we need σ(a^n) ≡ 1 (mod 2021).
