[INFO] 09-22 06:54:54 run_experiments.py:122] 
[INFO] 09-22 06:54:54 run_experiments.py:122] A saddle pair $(R, C)$ is called a minimal pair if for each saddle pair $\left(R^{\prime}, C^{\prime}\right)$ with $R^{\prime} \subseteq R$ and $C^{\prime} \subseteq C$, we have $R^{\prime}=R$ and $C^{\prime}=C$.
